tion":"Cliffs border most of the Smith","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/885478","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/885478"}},{"id":"885479","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"888266","description":"","caption":"Trails can be accessed from some of the camps","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/885479","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/885479"}},{"id":"885480","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"888267","description":"Camp sites must be registered with the ranger on launch day.  The order of group registration is determined by when the first person in your group signs up, the day before launch.  Camps have a pit toilet.","caption":"Camp Site Sign","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/885480","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/885480"}}],"detail":{"id":"1021","permitUrl":"http://stateparks.mt.gov/smith-river","permitInfo":"Permits issued through a lottery managed by Montana Fish, Wildlife, and Parks. Peak season is May 15th to July 15th. ","description":"Superb fishing, gorgeous scenery, and a remote setting combine to make a trip on the Smith River an unforgettable experience. With one put-in point and one take-out point, the 59-mile stretch of river is accessible only by canoe, raft, or other appropriate watercraft.\n\nBecause of its popularity, the Smith River is alone among Montana rivers to require a permit to float the waterway. A drawing for the permit is conducted each February; nine float parties are allowed to put in on the river each day. These regulations moderate fishing pressure and allow for long floats in relative solitude.\n\n